{
  "kind": "record-set",
  "record_set": "post-places",
  "what_this_is": "The places a person's posts can go (src/social-posts.mjs), one row each. A row names the direct publisher that posts there (`adapter`, a publisher of @opencoredev/social-sdk bound by name in src/post-publishers.mjs), the service-connections connection that reaches the person's account there (`connection_vendor`; its tokens stay in the person's locked box), how the publisher's options are filled from that connection (`options`: each leaf is { \"held\": field } for a value kept in the box, { \"plain\": field } for a field the connection keeps readable, { \"service_origin\": true } for this service's own address, or { \"value\": ... }), which account the post goes to (`account`), the only hosts a held value may be sent to (`hosts`: each a host name, or { \"plain\": field } for the host of the address a readable field of the connection holds, such as the person's own publication), whether a video goes as an address the place fetches or as its bytes (`media_from`: \"address\" or \"bytes\"), settings every post there starts with (`default_settings`), and what a post must be before that place takes it (`format`, read by src/post-ready.mjs): `caption_max_characters` for the words as sent (the link included; null when the place sets no limit of its own), `media_needed` when the place never posts words alone, `media_kinds` the kinds of file it takes (the first part of a file's type: video, image; an empty one means it takes words only), each with its own limits (`media_types`, `max_bytes`, `min_seconds`, `max_seconds`, `min_aspect`, `max_aspect` as width over height, and a `caption_max_characters` of its own), `settings` it needs or limits (`setting` as named in settings_by_platform, `name` in plain words, `needed`, `max_characters`, `refuses_characters`), and `source`, where those facts were read and when. `tool_id` names the Workshop tool that publishes a post to the place (tool:publish-a-post), so a place's publisher is a tool a person's AI can find, while the adapter module stays code. The rows are read through src/data-rows.mjs (kind post-place). A new place, or a managed service standing in for several, is a new row.",
